lete title of the book in which two James Beard Award winners recommended the restaurant where Ali Khan enjoyed a New Mexican staple in his cos\",\r\n  338\t  \"gold\": \"Five Hundred Things To Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\",\r\n  339\t  \"got\": \"500 Things to Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\",\r\n  340\t  \"secs\": 16.9,\r\n  341\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 500 Things to Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\\n\\n\",\r\n  342\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  343\t },\r\n  344\t {\r\n  345\t  \"task_id\": \"dc28cf18-6431-458b-83ef-64b3ce566c10\",\r\n  346\t  \"question\": \"My family reunion is this week, and I was assigned the mashed potatoes to bring. The attendees include my married mother and father, my twin brother and his fam\",\r\n  347\t  \"gold\": \"2\",\r\n  348\t  \"got\": \"2\",\r\n  349\t  \"secs\": 11.3,\r\n  350\t  \"raw_tail\": \"erage potato is about half a pound, and potatoes are sold in 5-pound bags.\\\"\\n* Total weight of potatoes needed = $18 \\\\text{ potatoes} \\\\times 0.5 \\\\text{ lbs/potato} = 9 \\\\text{ pounds}$.\\n* Bag size = 5 pounds per bag.\\n* Number of bags = $9 / 5 = 1.8$ bags.\\n* Since you need whole bags (\\\"How many whole bags of potatoes do I need?\\\"), you must round up to the next whole bag, which is 2 bags.\\n\\nANSWER: 2\\n\\n\",\r\n  351\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  352\t },\r\n  353\t {\r\n  354\t  \"task_id\": \"e142056d-56ab-4352-b091-b56054bd1359\",\r\n  355\t  \"question\": \"Bob was invited to participate in a game show, and he advanced to the final round. The final round offered Bob the chance to win a large sum by playing a game a\",\r\n  356\t  \"gold\": \"16000\",\r\n  357\t  \"got\": \"16000\",\r\n  358\t  \"secs\": 19.7,\r\n  359\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 16000\\n\\n\\n[tool websearch {}]\\n\\n[tool websearch {\\\"query\\\":\\\"Bob was invited to participate in a game show and he advanced to the final round 30 shiny ]\\n\",\r\n  360\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  361\t },\r\n  362\t {\r\n  363\t  \"task_id\": \"e1fc63a2-da7a-432f-be78-7c4a95598703\",\r\n  364\t  \"question\": \"If Eliud Kipchoge could maintain his record-making marathon pace indefinitely, how many thousand hours would it take him to run the distance between the Earth a\",\r\n  365\t  \"gold\": \"17\",\r\n  366\t  \"got\": \"\",\r\n  367\t  \"secs\": 7.4,\r\n  368\t  \"raw_tail\": \"\\n\",\r\n  369\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  370\t },\r\n  371\t {\r\n  372\t  \"task_id\": \"ec09fa32-d03f-4bf8-84b0-1f16922c3ae4\",\r\n  373\t  \"question\": \"Here's a fun riddle that I think you'll enjoy.\\n\\nYou have been selected to play the final round of the hit new game show \\\"Pick That Ping-Pong\\\". In this round, yo\",\r\n  374\t  \"gold\": \"3\",\r\n  375\t  \"got\": \"3\",\r\n  376\t  \"secs\": 15.2,\r\n  377\t  \"raw_tail\": \"To maximize your odds of winning the grand prize, you should choose ball **3**.\\n\\nANSWER: 3\\n\\n\",\r\n  378\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  379\t }\r\n  380\t]","toolCallId":"call_b8d7bfe5c9e14b3bac10f6d3","name":"read"}
